<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">South Carolina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">South Carolina is a region of the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a> River and North Carolina. It was home to Mississippian chiefdoms such as Cofitachequi and saw a short-lived French fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlesfort">Charlesfort</a> in 1562. English settlers founded Charles Town in 1670, creating a plantation colony worked by enslaved Africans. In 1860 it was the first state to secede, triggering the formation of the Confederacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-carolina.jpg" alt="South Carolina" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Design by South Carolina General Assembly, SVG by Steve Hall · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Carolina.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
